== guard against a sentinel that is reassigned in func init(), applied to the result of a promoted method.
Go semantics: engine.ErrClosed never leaves Alive; kverr.errInternal and the channel error (unresolved(memory)) do.
errtrace treats ErrClosed as unstable (two loads may differ), so it keeps all 3 of Ping's entries and marks each 'possibly handled':
ErrClosed ("is reassigned outside its initialization"), errInternal ("may be the same value as engine.ErrClosed") and the unresolved value.
This is the documented conservative behaviour (plan P07, e2e guards/eq_unstable_sentinel); the entry that matters is that nothing is dropped.
-- args --
repo/repo.go:@alive
